    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of a square with a given perimeter, we need to first determine the length of one side of the square. \n\nGiven that the perimeter of the square is 32 feet, it means that the sum of all four sides equals 32 feet.\n\nLet's denote the length of one side of the square as 's'. \n\nPerimeter = 4 * s (since a square has four equal sides)\n\n32 = 4 * s\n\nDivide both sides of the equation by 4 to solve for s:\n\ns = 32 / 4\n\ns = 8\n\nSo, the length of one side of the square is 8 feet.\n\nNow that we know the length of one side, we can find the area of the square. \n\nArea of a square = side × side\n\nA = s × s\n\nA = 8 × 8\n\nA = 64 square feet.\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\boxed{64}.",
