    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to find the length of one side. We know that the perimeter of a square is equal to the sum of all its sides. Since all sides of a square are equal in length, we can write:\n\nPerimeter = 4 * length\n\nGiven the perimeter:\n\nPerimeter = 32ft\n\nNow, we can solve for the length of one side:\n\nlength = Perimeter / 4\nlength = 32ft / 4\nlength = 8ft\n\nNext, we use the computed length to calculate the area of the square. The formula for the area of a square is:\n\nArea = side^2\n\nFor this square, the area is:\n\nArea = side^2\nArea = 8ft * 8ft\nArea = 64 square feet",
